2. Five-Day Evaluation Grant

Subject to the terms below, the copyright holder ("Licensor") may grant an individual
or organization a temporary, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable right to use
the Software for evaluation, academic testing, and non-commercial research purposes.

Each separate evaluation authorization is valid for five (5) consecutive calendar
days only.

The five-day period begins on the date specified by the Licensor when the evaluation
authorization is issued. If no date is specified, the period begins on the first day
the recipient downloads, runs, or otherwise uses the Software, whichever occurs first.

A new five-day evaluation period requires a new authorization from the Licensor.
Downloading, cloning, reinstalling, copying, modifying, or rebuilding the Software
does not automatically create a new evaluation period.

3. Permitted Activities During the Evaluation Period

During a valid five-day evaluation period, the recipient may:

a. inspect and study the source code;
b. run the Software for evaluation and non-commercial academic/research testing;
c. modify the Software locally for the same evaluation purpose; and
d. create temporary local copies reasonably necessary for that evaluation.

